Z||000003||Greg Piet||07-03-2001||03:53 PM||||I know that my cam works in my 3.1 and the guy at the shop im referring will et you know if it works in a 2.8, but its not Crane...<BR>It is Clevite, and I LOVE IT!<P>It is the "Phase 2" cam at <A HREF="http://www.engine-parts.com/gmv6/camspecs.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.engine-parts.com/gmv6/camspecs.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 SM<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">    <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||07-03-2001||09:57 PM||||The camshaft will work with your 2.8 but the question should be what kind of power would it make. Bigger is not always better especially when you have a street machine with stock type heads and exhaust. I don’t know what you are planing but maybe I can help in some way here so here it goes. <P>I ran the numbers for you in the Dyno program to give you an idea of what kind of power curve you should get from this camshaft with ported manifolds and stock type heads. <P>They are,<BR>RPM...horsepower...torque<BR>2000...49...129<BR>2500...66...139<BR>3000...87...152<BR>3500...107..161<BR>4000...125..165<BR>4500...139..162<BR>5000...149..156<BR>5500...152..145<BR>6000...149..131<BR>6500...139..112<P>Here is what the stock fiero engine power curve looks like with ported manifolds in my program for your comparison.<P>RPM...horsepower...torque<BR>2000...62...164<BR>2500...81...170<BR>3000...102..180<BR>3500...121..181<BR>4000...135..177<BR>4500...143..167<BR>5000...145..152<BR>5500...138..132<BR>6000...126..110<BR>6500...110..88<P>I think the Crane PowerMax H-260-2 is one of the best street cams for a 2.8/3.1/3.4 engine, especially the 2.8 if you want more top-end. The power output looks like this in a 2.8-liter engine with ported manifolds.<P>2000...59...155<BR>2500...77...161<BR>3000...98...172<BR>3500...118..177<BR>4000...135..178<BR>4500...147..172<BR>5000...155..163<BR>5500...157..150<BR>6000...152..133<BR>6500...140..113<P>The Crane PowerMax camshaft would give you better acceleration and overall better performance than the one you are looking at for a street car. <P><BR> <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-03-2001).]||||reg||1
